# 🌸 Flower Classification Using Machine Learning

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on classifying Iris flowers into three different species using Machine Learning algorithms.

The system uses flower measurements to predict the species of an Iris flower.

The three flower species are:
- Iris Setosa
- Iris Versicolor
- Iris Virginica

## 🎯 Objectives

- Load and understand the Iris dataset.
- Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA).
- Visualize feature relationships using different graphs.
- Train Machine Learning classification models.
- Evaluate model performance.
- Predict flower species for new user inputs.

## 📊 Dataset Description

This project uses the built-in Iris dataset from Scikit-learn.

The dataset contains 150 records and 4 input features.

**Features:**
- Sepal Length (cm)
- Sepal Width (cm)
- Petal Length (cm)
- Petal Width (cm)

**Target Variable:**
- Species

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Joblib

## 🤖 Machine Learning Algorithms

Two classification algorithms are implemented:

1. Logistic Regression
2. Decision Tree Classifier

Both models are trained and evaluated to compare their performance.

## 🔍 Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

The following visualizations are created:

- Histogram
- Species Distribution Bar Chart
- Scatter Plot
- Box Plot
- Pair Plot
- Correlation Heatmap

## 📈 Model Evaluation

The models are evaluated using:

- Accuracy Score
- Confusion Matrix
- Precision
- Recall
- F1-Score

A model accuracy comparison graph is also generated.

## 🌸 Flower Prediction System

A prediction system is developed using the trained Logistic Regression model.

Users can enter four flower measurements:

- Sepal Length
- Sepal Width
- Petal Length
- Petal Width

The system predicts the corresponding flower species.

